          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Early Life and Education</strong><br>\nNoam Chomsky was born in 1928 in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania. Growing up during the Great Depression influenced his political thought and led to his lifelong activism. He was drawn to linguistics from a young age, which laid the foundation for his future as a leading academic.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Revolutionizing Linguistics</strong><br>\nChomsky revolutionized the field of linguistics by introducing the theory of generative grammar, which proposes that the ability to understand and produce language is innate to humans. His 1957 book \"Syntactic Structures\" broke new ground in the study of linguistics.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Chomsky's Political Activism</strong><br>\nApart from his academic pursuits, Chomsky is well-known for his political activism. He has been a vocal critic of U.S. foreign policy, mainstream media, and capitalism, advocating for social justice and a more equitable world order.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          }
        ],
        "slideBackgroundSelector": {}
      },
      {
        "elements": [
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
