            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>The Chomsky Hierarchy</strong><br>\nIn computer science and linguistics, the Chomsky hierarchy classifies languages according to their generative power. This has had significant implications for the development of programming languages and the understanding of the human brain's language-processing capabilities.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Media Critique and the Propaganda Model</strong><br>\nChomsky co-authored \"Manufacturing Consent,\" which argues that the mass media act as a propaganda system for elite interests. According to Chomsky, the media operates through five filters that shape the news, often aligning with powerful societal interests.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Contributions to Philosophy</strong><br>\nChomsky's influence extends to philosophy, especially in the philosophy of language and mind. His ideas challenge behaviorist notions, arguing for an inherent human nature and the existence of a universal grammar common to all languages.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
