            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Later Works and Ideas</strong><br>\nChomsky has continued to publish on linguistics, politics, and philosophy well into the 21st century. His later works delve into the repercussions of globalization, the persistence of imperial power structures, and the dangers they pose to democracy.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Chomsky's Educational Impact</strong><br>\nChomsky's teaching career at MIT has influenced generations of students. His pedagogical approach emphasizes critical thinking and skepticism, encouraging students to question authority and received wisdom.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Continuing Legacy</strong><br>\nAs of my knowledge cutoff in 2023, Chomsky remains an active public intellectual, writing, lecturing, and participating in political discourse. His work continues to inspire those who seek to understand the complexities of language, thought, and power. His lifelong commitment to humanistic values stands as a testament to his intellectual breadth and civic engagement.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
